// The two matmuls of the hyper-connection block, each with the glue around it
// folded into its epilogue. LLM.md L2a made this the first kernel of the
// vertical: the block is over half of llama.cpp's prefill graph (30.6%
// elementwise glue + 12.2% tiny-N F32 matmul + ~7% for this pair), and almost
// none of that is arithmetic.
//
//   MODE 0   [lowRank + hc, wide] * xn  ->  silu(lo/hc) fp16, and inject fp32
//   MODE 1   [wide, lowRank] * lo       ->  sigmoid, collapsed into mixed
//
// MODE 0 is the fusion L2a costed. `w_inject` is a [10240, 4] F32 matrix
// applied to the *same* xn that `w_down` reads, and llama.cpp runs it as its
