15	//
16	// One workgroup is one (token, stream), which is what makes every reduction
17	// here workgroup-local: three of them in sequence over 2560 values — the key's
18	// sum of squares and the query's together, then the dot product of the two
19	// normalised vectors, then the gated value's. llama.cpp spends two RMS_NORMs,
20	// two MULs, a SUM_ROWS, a SCALE, an ABS, a CLAMP, a SQRT, an SGN, a MUL, a
21	// SIGMOID, a REPEAT, a MUL and a third RMS_NORM_MUL on the same thing.
22	//
23	// The signed square root is the unusual step and it is not a normalisation: a
24	// dot product of two 2560-wide normalised vectors is too wide for a sigmoid to
25	// resolve, and sqrt compresses it while sgn keeps the sign it would otherwise
26	// lose. ggml_sgn(0) is 0, so a zero score gates at exactly 0.5 — which is why
27	// the clamp's floor never reaches the sign.
